    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> alexcrichton submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15148#pullrequestreview-5773347466\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 637593038,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793815758
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15148#discussion_r4471382738\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I realize we're a bit inconsistent on this, but I think this option would suffice being ungated entirely. The actual definition of <code>wasmtime_config_wasm_stack_switching_set</code> in Rust has no #[cfg] for example so there's no need to gate this.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 637593042,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793815758
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> dhil submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15148#pullrequestreview-5773632955\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 637598134,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793816997
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> dhil created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15148#discussion_r4471609931\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Ah excellent. So I can remove the cargo feature. We still need to gate on the GC feature in the C and C++ right?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 637598135,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793816998
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> alexcrichton submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15148#pullrequestreview-5773660507\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 637598642,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793817119
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15148#discussion_r4471630317\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Given that it's a cargo feature on the <code>wasmtime</code> crate itself I think keeping the feature infrastructure still makes sense. That way support can still be tested and reflected upon and/or customized during builds.</p>\n<p>We can probably clean up GC-related guards at some point, but basically the <code>#ifdef</code> in headers should match the <code>#[cfg]</code> in the Rust source itself. </p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 637598645,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793817119
    },
